# list[k] = k * slope: the counter runs as a 64-bit integer, which also addresses the element, and each turn converts it to a double for the product. Eight turns are eight conversions, eight multiplications, eight stores.
# HOT-LABEL: steps by 8
# HOT: Int64 b@[[k]] = Phi(
# HOT: Double b@[[number]] = IToD(b@[[k]], {{*}}:Mul)
# HOT-NEXT: Double b@[[product]] = Mul(b@[[number]], b@[[slope]], {{*}}:Mul)
# HOT: Store(b@[[product]], b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Writes:TypedArrayElements
# REPEAT: turn = 1..7
# HOT: Int64 b@[[k%(turn)]] = Add(b@[[k]], $%(turn)(b@{{*}}), {{*}}:Increment)
# HOT-NEXT: Double b@[[number%(turn)]] = IToD(b@[[k%(turn)]], {{*}}:Mul)
# HOT-NEXT: Double b@[[product%(turn)]] = Mul(b@[[slope]], b@[[number%(turn)]], {{*}}:Mul)
# HOT: Store(b@[[product%(turn)]], b@{{*}}, offset = %(turn*8), ControlDependent|Writes:TypedArrayElements
# END REPEAT
# HOT-LABEL: end of loop
# The only branch is the loop condition, and no product is tested for NaN ahead of its store.
